---
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import Link from "../components/Link.astro";
import { vendorSections } from "../components/privacy/privacyPolicyModel";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, DOMAIN, ORGANISATION, POSTAL_ADDRESS } from "../lib/privacy/organisation";
import { VENDORS } from "../lib/privacy/registry";

const vendors = vendorSections();
const hosting = VENDORS["github-pages"];
const analytics = VENDORS["google-analytics"];
---

<LegalPage title="Privacy policy" description={`How ${DOMAIN} handles personal data, who we share it with, and your rights.`}>
	<h2>Who we are</h2>
	<p>
		{ORGANISATION} ("we", "us") runs {DOMAIN}, a collection of writing tools. To ask us anything about your data,
		email <Link href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</Link> or write to us at {POSTAL_ADDRESS}.
	</p>

	<h2>Children</h2>
	<p>
		This site is not directed at children, and we don't knowingly collect personal data from children under 13. If we
		learn that we have, we will delete it.
	</p>

	<h2>What we don't do</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			There are no accounts. We never ask for your name, and we only have your email address if you give it to us.
		</li>
		<li>We don't show advertising or track you across other websites.</li>
		<li>We don't sell your data.</li>
		<li>We don't use personal data to train AI models.</li>
		<li>
			Our tools don't send us what you write. It stays on your device, and when a tool makes a share link, the link
			carries your text after the <code>#</code> in the address, which browsers never send to a server. The only writing
			we receive is what you choose to send us in a form.
		</li>
		<li>
			We don't receive your phone's motion. The Magic 8 Ball reads it on the page, only to notice a shake, and only
			once you allow it where your device asks. The readings are never stored or sent.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Hosting</h2>
	<p>
		{hosting.name} serves this site. When you visit, {hosting.name} logs your IP address for security and to keep the
		service running, as described in <Link href={hosting.privacyUrl}>its privacy statement</Link>. Our legal basis is
		legitimate interest: a website can't be delivered or protected without this. GitHub keeps these logs; we don't receive them.
	</p>

	<h2>Analytics</h2>
	<p>
		If you accept, we use {analytics.name} to understand which pages, tools and settings people use, so we know what to improve.
		Our legal basis is your consent. Nothing is loaded until you accept, and you can withdraw consent at any time.
	</p>
	<p>
		In plain terms, we record which pages you visit, which tool settings you use, roughly how long your text is (in ranges of word counts),
		how you reach the site, how long you use a tool, and your device type. For the Magic 8 Ball, we record whether you typed a question, but never the question itself. We never record what you write.
		{analytics.name} also measures some things itself: how far down a page you scroll, which links to other sites you
		follow, when you start and submit a form (never what you type into it), and any file downloads and video plays.
		Google also receives what it collects automatically, such as your IP address and browser details. For the cookies
		involved and how long they last, see the <Link href="/cookie-policy">cookie policy</Link>.
	</p>
	<p>
		We have linked {analytics.name} to Google Search Console, which shows us which Google searches lead people to this site.
		The link works both ways: Search Console's search statistics appear in our analytics reports, and aggregate site
		statistics from {analytics.name}, such as how many people visit a page, are shared with Search Console. Neither product
		is told who any individual visitor is.
	</p>
	<p><Button variant="secondary" data-open-cookie-settings>Change your cookie settings</Button></p>

	<h2 id="waitlists-and-forms">Waitlists and forms</h2>
	<p>
		Some pages invite you to join a waitlist or answer a few questions, for example to hear when a tool or feature is
		ready. Every form is optional, says what it's for, and sends nothing to us until you submit.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you give us your email address, we keep it with a note of which form you used and when, so we only email you
		about what you asked about. If a form offers extra options, such as trying an early version, we only act on the
		ones you tick. Joining one waitlist never signs you up for another.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you answer optional questions, we read your answers to decide what to build and how. We don't publish them or
		quote them anywhere without asking you first. Some questions may invite you to describe your own writing. Share
		only what you're comfortable sending us.
	</p>
	<p>
		Our legal basis is your consent, which you give separately for each form and each option you tick. Cloudflare
		stores what you send in the EU on our behalf. It sees your IP address while handling the request and uses it to
		block abuse, but we don't store it with your details. When we email you, the email goes through our email provider.
		We don't add you to any other mailing list or share your address with anyone else.
	</p>
	<p>
		To leave a waitlist, reply to any email from us or write to <Link href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}
			>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</Link
		>. You can withdraw from one form or one option and keep the rest, or ask us to delete everything you've sent us.
	</p>

	<h2>Who we share data with</h2>
	<ul class="vendors">
		{
			vendors.map((vendor) => (
				<li>
					<strong>{vendor.name}</strong> ({vendor.category}). {vendor.roleDescription}{" "}
					<Link href={vendor.privacyUrl}>Privacy policy</Link>
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>

	<p>We may also disclose personal data:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>To comply with the law, a court order or a government or regulatory request.</li>
		<li>To protect the rights, property or safety of us, our users or others.</li>
		<li>To a successor, if we are part of a merger, acquisition or sale of assets.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>International transfers</h2>
	<p>These companies may process data outside your country. We rely on the following safeguards:</p>
	<ul>
		{
			vendors.map((vendor) => (
				<li>
					{vendor.name}: {vendor.transfer}
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>
	<p>
		Depending on where you live, you may be able to ask us for access to the personal data we hold about you, to correct
		or delete it, to restrict or object to how we use it, to receive a portable copy, and to withdraw your consent. If
		you are in the EU or UK, you can also complain to your local data protection authority. We don't sell personal data
		or use it for targeted advertising, so there is nothing to opt out of.
	</p>
	<p>
		To exercise a right, email <Link href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</Link>. Analytics data is linked
		only to a random ID stored in your browser, not to your name, so we usually can't find one person's data. If you want us to
		try, tell us the value of the <code>_ga</code> cookie from your browser. Turning analytics off in the cookie settings
		stops any further collection. For anything you sent us in a form, write from the email address you gave us, so we
		can find your details.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you are in the EU or UK, our legal bases are your consent for analytics and for forms, and our legitimate
		interest in running and securing the site for hosting. If a browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we treat it as a refusal of
		analytics. We don't respond to Do Not Track, as there is no common standard for it.
	</p>

	<h2>Security</h2>
	<p>
		We use reasonable measures to protect personal data from loss and unauthorised access. No system is completely secure, so we can't guarantee the security of
		anything sent over the internet.
	</p>

	<h2>How long we keep data</h2>
	<p>
		We keep personal data only as long as we need it for the purposes above. The cookies we set last as long as the{" "}
		<Link href="/cookie-policy">cookie policy</Link> says, and you can delete them at any time in your browser.
	</p>
	<p>
		{analytics.name} deletes the record of each event, such as a page view, after 2 months, and data linked to the random ID
		in your browser after 14 months. The totals in its reports, such as how many people visited a page, are kept longer
		but aren't linked to you.
	</p>
	<p>
		We keep what you send through a form, your email address and any answers, until we've sent what you asked for, such
		as the email saying a tool has launched. If we decide not to build it, we'll tell you and delete it then. You can
		ask us to delete it sooner at any time.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>We update this page when what we collect or who we share it with changes. The date at the top shows the latest change.</p>
</LegalPage>

<style>
	ul {
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
		padding-inline-start: var(--space-6);
	}
	li {
		margin-block-end: var(--space-2);
	}
</style>
